  "question": {
    "text": "A conducting loop of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>10</mn><msqrt><mi>&#960;</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> is placed perpendicular to a uniform magnetic field of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>. The magnetic field is decreased to zero in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> at a steady rate. The induced emf in the circular loop at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>emf</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>mV</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>emf</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>mV</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>emf</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mi>mV</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>emf</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>mV</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>at</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>.</p><p>Magnetic field will decrease linearly as given below. We can say, value of magnetic field at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>will&#160;be</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn></math>.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0058_b485036f8b1d.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 245px;\" /></p><p>Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mtext>ind&#160;</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>&#981;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#916;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#916;</mi><mfenced><mi>B</mi></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>10</mn><msqrt><mi>&#960;</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>01</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mV</mi></math></p>"
  }
